        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: جمجمة",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جمجمة — jumjuma — \"a skull\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "الجمجمة تحمي الدماغ. al-jumjuma taḥmī ad-dimāgh. The skull protects the brain."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: جماجم, jamājim."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جمجمة (jumjuma) is a native Arabic word on a doubled four-letter shape, j-m-j-m. EtymDB sets it beside Hebrew gulgolet and Aramaic gulgaltā, \"a skull\", but how they are related is not settled. Its plural jamājim follows the usual four-letter pattern."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
